  "summary": "ACLU roundup of Flock developments: ACLU of Massachusetts open-records work shows Flock's default contract lets the company share agency data for 'investigative purposes' even when departments restrict sharing; Virginia reporting reveals Warren County (VA) Sheriff's Office did the most ICE-related Flock searches in the state; a Texas department's abortion-related search was misrepresented; and Flock has partnered with Ring and is marketing drone-as-first-responder services to private businesses.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Flock's default agreement with police departments gives the company the right to share data with federal and local agencies for \"investigative purposes\" even if a local department chooses to restrict data to its own officers.",
